/target
# Cargo.lock IS tracked. kinference ships as a binary (and as a container image), so
# the lockfile is what makes a build reproducible — without it, `cargo build` on
# a different day silently resolves different dependency versions than the ones
# that were tested. The ignore-the-lockfile convention is for libraries, whose
# consumers do their own resolution.
aws-harness/config.toml
.*.swp
